WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.360
Speaker 1: Good news out of Michigan, where
under the leadership of Democratic Governor

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:10.690
Gretchen Whitmer, Michigan has repealed an
insane 1931 abortion ban.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.870
This is really wacky stuff.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.110
The Detroit Free Press reports.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:20.760
Whitmer repeals Michigan's 1931 abortion ban
with the stroke of a pen.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.690
Governor Gretchen Whitmer repealed an unenforceable
Michigan law Wednesday that makes it a felony

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:30.050
to administer most abortions, with no exception
for rape or incest.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:34.160
Now, unenforceable, unenforceable is a critical
word here.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.520
And so the reason to do this is less about
the idea that that law would start to be enforced

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:45.760
right now, but the idea that it could be enforced
depending on what continues to happen at the

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.870
highest court of the land, the Supreme Court
in the United States.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:53.690
And this is a very, very good thing.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:59.940
It is important to understand that this is
only the beginning of what is certain to be

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:08.710
a much longer, I guess we would call it crusade
against abortion that started decades ago

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.330
with the passage of Roe v Wade.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:17.759
Roe v Wade was about ensuring right to an
abortion, but it triggered the battle against

00:01:17.759 --> 00:01:19.890
abortion from the American right.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:25.160
They had a major success recently when the
Supreme Court did away with Roe v Wade.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.480
And we know that it is only the beginning.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.450
Here is Governor Gretchen Whitmer officially
signing a repeal of that abortion ban.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:37.440
Speaker 2: That's what I about.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.780
Speaker 1: All right.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:43.540
So most of us understand what it looks like
to sign a piece of paper.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.640
And here is Gretchen Whitmer actually saying
something about this just ahead of the signing.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.329
Speaker 2: I don't ever want someone from
the press to ask me again, should we talk

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:52.600
about abortion or the economy?

00:01:52.600 --> 00:02:00.000
If you don't think abortion is about the economy,
you might not have a uterus.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.450
Right?

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:08.160
We know that the decision when and whether
or not to bear a child is the most consequential

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.750
decision economically that a family or a woman
will make in her lifetime.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.440
The government has no business getting in
the way of conversations between women and

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.440
their doctors.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.879
Speaker 1: This should not really be controversial,
but it did send the American right into a

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:26.550
tizzy, hurling the term Marxist at Gretchen
Whitmer.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:27.550
I don't know why.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:28.550
I don't know why.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:32.500
Getting rid of an insane law from 1931 makes
you a marxist in 2023.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.670
I don't think they know either.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:36.099
I don't think they know what Marxist even
means.

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:41.070
But that doesn't matter, because what we do
see is their passion.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:47.550
If you want to use that word for making it
as difficult as possible to get an abortion

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:52.010
under any circumstances and anywhere in the
United States.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:54.070
And so this is a small step.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:58.830
Again, at this point, this was an unenforceable
1931 law.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:02.080
But it is still important to get these laws
off the books.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:08.060
And many states, particularly red states,
have these retrograde ancient laws on the

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.700
books, even if they aren't being enforced
right now.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:15.959
Any one of these that can be taken off the
table in terms of possible future enforcement

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:17.799
should be considered a win.

00:03:17.799 --> 00:03:25.340
And remember, Governor Gretchen Whitmer, easily,
easily winning reelection in November, despite

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:32.840
a challenge from Trump endorsed MAGA candidate
Tudor Dickson, who went down in flames.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.980
And we can all be very, very happy about that.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.560
We'll continue following this fight for just
simple medical rights.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.189
That's what we're talking about here.

